cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Monograph PDF"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mun"
    given-names: "Aung Ye"
    email: "aungyemun25@gmail.com"
version: "0.4.1"
date-released: "2026-10-23"
license: "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aungyemun/monograph-pdf"
abstract: >
  An offline desktop application for viewing, editing, organizing, converting,
  protecting and signing PDF documents. Supports form filling and design, text
  and image editing, merge/split/rotate, layout-preserving PDF to Word
  conversion, Office and image to PDF, AES-256 password protection with
  permissions, watermarks, visual signatures, true redaction and offline OCR
  (English and Japanese). Monograph PDF itself makes no network connections on
  Windows 10/11; optional Office conversion uses a locally installed suite.
keywords:
  - PDF
  - PDF editor
  - PDF forms
  - PDF to Word
  - document conversion
  - OCR
  - Windows
  - offline
